Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Part 1: ", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0037521981806793`*^9, 4.003752226963936*^9}, 
   4.0037522569801636`*^9, 
   4.0042747834287567`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4ddb49c0-69ab-f74f-b898-\
ac1a7e7949ca"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Subsection 1.1:", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.003752246619238*^9, 
  4.003752260865383*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b14d9a0d-b3e2-184a-87df-\
975829b803cb"],

Cell["\<\
Question

Use FeynArts and FeynCalc with the real-scalar \[CurlyPhi]\:2074 model [S] to \
generate all one-loop 1PI two-point and four-point diagrams and their \
amplitudes. Include the relevant package commands, label momenta, determine \
symmetry factors, identify the three four-point channels, and give the \
converted integrands and their ToPaVe forms, together with the Wick-rotation \
and loop-measure conventions.

Physics overview

In perturbation theory, Feynman diagrams organize the contributions to \
correlation functions. External lines represent the fields whose interaction \
is being studied, internal lines represent propagators, and vertices \
represent interactions from the action. The diagrams contributing to the \
proper vertex functions are the one-particle irreducible (1PI) diagrams: they \
cannot be split into two disconnected parts by cutting one internal line.

For real \[CurlyPhi]\:2074 theory, the one-loop two-point function has a \
tadpole diagram. Two external legs meet at one quartic vertex, while the \
remaining two legs form an internal loop. The one-loop four-point function \
has a bubble diagram: two quartic vertices are connected by two internal \
propagators, with two external legs attached to each vertex.

There are three inequivalent ways to pair the four external legs. They \
correspond to the channel momenta P\:2081\:2082, P\:2081\:2083, and P\:2081\
\:2084. These are conventionally called the s-, t-, and u-type channels, \
respectively. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.003832750978258*^9, {4.0038329863285294`*^9, 4.0038329991137753`*^9}, {
   4.0038332178311462`*^9, 4.0038332225398808`*^9}, {4.003833321805994*^9, 
   4.003833321805994*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5d882076-a6fb-aa4f-a19e-\
cec35cdca447"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"tadpole", "=", 
    RowBox[{"InsertFields", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"CreateTopologies", "[", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", 
        RowBox[{"1", "->", "1"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"S", "[", "1", "]"}], "}"}], "->", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"S", "[", "1", "]"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"InsertionLevel", "->", 
       RowBox[{"{", "Classes", "}"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Model", "->", 
       RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"modelDir", ",", "\"\<Phi4\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"GenericModel", "->", 
       RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"modelDir", ",", "\"\<Phi4\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}],
    ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Paint", "[", 
  RowBox[{"tadpole", ",", 
   RowBox[{"Numbering", "->", "Simple"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"FieldNumbers", "->", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0038448764019737`*^9, 4.0038448764019737`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d8289922-8fec-334b-97ee-c5d9aeffd88d"],

