Cell[TextData[{
 " Amplitude Generation and Derivation Strategy\n\nThe one-loop 1PI proper \
vertices are determined by applying the Feynman rules in Euclidean signature. \
The 1PI two-point function receives a single tadpole contribution, while the \
four-point function receives bubble contributions across three distinct \
kinematic channels.\n\n1.Tadpole Amplitude (Two-Point Function): The tadpole \
topology arises from contracting two legs of the $\\phi^4$ interaction. The \
combinatorics of contracting 4 identical fields yields a symmetry factor of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["S", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "1", "/", "2"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "$S = 1/2$", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7caea365-0fd0-844a-82ef-9fa41d13d1b4"],
 ". The loop momentum $q$ flows through a single internal line of mass $m$ \
with propagator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
            SuperscriptBox[
             StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
            SuperscriptBox[
             StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}], "-1"], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "$(q^2 + m^2)^{-1}$", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c6704c92-dd90-184e-9849-8021ce1e86ae"],
 ", completely independent of external momentum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "$p$", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "97eebadd-fa59-0d49-8931-e7a37e7a1177"],
 ":\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"1", "-", "loop"}], 
      RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}]], "(", 
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["\[Lambda]", "2"], 
     RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
         StyleBox["q", "TI"]}], 
        SuperscriptBox[
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]"}], ")"}], 
         StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], 
       FractionBox["1", 
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"]}]]}]}]}], "\[Congruent]", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["\[Lambda]", "2"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], "    ", "[", 
      RowBox[{"B", "-", "01"}], "]"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b14c8ab8-69ef-c64e-bae2-1a9d8ed885a2"],
 "\n2. Bubble Amplitudes (Four-Point Function): Each bubble graph involves \
two quartic vertices connected by two internal propagators. Exchanging the \
two propagators gives a symmetry factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["S", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "1", "/", "2"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "$S = 1/2$", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "43f0d08f-b1c6-bb42-981c-075d66af0a94"],
 " for each channel. With incoming external momenta ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["p", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"], ",", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["p", "TI"], "3"], ",", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["p", "TI"], "4"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "$p_1, p_2, p_3, p_4$", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f5725cc0-35c2-404b-a5f3-7c7e44b4c7fa"],
 " satisfying ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Sum]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "$\\sum p_i = 0$", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "29f1068e-6067-cf44-95f7-3951e2ae7afd"],
 ", the external legs can attach to the two vertices in three topologically \
inequivalent pairings. These define the three Mandelstam-like transfer \
channels: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], "12"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["p", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "$P_{12} = p_1 + p_2$", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0789db09-fdb1-8d4c-acd9-1f5411f25f4e"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], "13"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["p", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["p", "TI"], "3"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "$P_{13} = p_1 + p_3$", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "35374fa9-0bc9-4441-b70c-347b649f9141"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], "14"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["p", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["p", "TI"], "4"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "$P_{14} = p_1 + p_4$", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e0ddecf3-6a2e-ce4e-a220-f1c86dca2196"],
 ".\nSumming over the three channels yields:\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"1", "-", "loop"}], 
      RowBox[{"(", "4", ")"}]], "(", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"]], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "2"], "2"], "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["B", "TI"], "(", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], "12"], ")"}], "+", 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["B", "TI"], "(", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], "13"], ")"}], "+", 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["B", "TI"], "(", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], "14"], ")"}]}], "]"}], "    ", "[", 
      RowBox[{"B", "-", "02"}], "]"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b6a46fc9-b9d0-2940-9e0c-1dc409982e97"],
 "\nwhere the scalar two-point bubble integral is defined by:\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], "(", 
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
        StyleBox["q", "TI"]}], 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]"}], ")"}], 
        StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], 
      FractionBox["1", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          SuperscriptBox[
           StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
          SuperscriptBox[
           StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}], 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          SuperscriptBox[
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             StyleBox["q", "TI"], "+", 
             StyleBox["P", "TI"]}], ")"}], "2"], "+", 
          SuperscriptBox[
           StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}]}]]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"b86c9eef-5d96-174f-8e74-a72e68547f4c"],
 "\nIn the code cells below, FeynArts generates these exact diagrammatic \
topologies, and FeynCalc converts the loop integrals into standard Passarino\
\[Dash]Veltman form: the tadpole reduces to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["A", "TI"], "0"], "(", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "$A_0(m^2)$", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cae6d0c3-181c-a240-b0f9-8b4aefa88a87"],
 ", and each bubble channel reduces to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["B", "TI"], "0"], "(", 
         RowBox[{
           SubsuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
            RowBox[{
              StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["j", "TI"]}], "2"], ",", 
           SuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"], ",", 
           SuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "$B_0(P_{ij}^2, m^2, m^2)$", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "27c72649-e66d-0844-a67a-2d7dc1d70b0e"],
 ", directly confirming our derivations [B-01] and [B-02]."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.0038470774433613`*^9, 4.003849363568001*^9, {4.0038496670441685`*^9, 
   4.003849669848049*^9}, {4.0038497023878784`*^9, 4.003849862871666*^9}, {
   4.0038499758446503`*^9, 
   4.003850010365549*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"91946d71-5988-384c-a6b8-\
749fd1da9f1d"],

