Cell["\<\
Question | Derive the one-loop MS beta function and its Wilson\[Dash]Fisher \
fixed point, establish the one-loop field counterterm, and explain why the \
tadpole cannot change the momentum exponent, distinguishing MS from the \
finite subtraction conditions in subsection 1.3.

Derivation | Minimal subtraction extracts only the pole part of the bubble \
integrals, yielding the coupling counterterm relation B-25. Differentiating \
at fixed bare parameters produces the beta function B-27, whose root gives \
the Wilson\[Dash]Fisher fixed point B-28. The one-loop tadpole self-energy is \
momentum-independent, so its divergence is absorbed entirely into the mass \
counterterm rather than a kinetic term, yielding a vanishing one-loop field \
counterterm B-29 and no change to the momentum exponent B-30.

Check | The fixed-bare differentiation algebra, series coefficients, and WF \
fixed point root are verified analytically and confirmed via minimal \
Mathematica code validating the beta equation and the vanishing derivative \
with respect to external momentum.

Anchor IDs | B-25\[Dash]B-30.

Status | derived and Mathematica checked.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.004274771730526*^9},ExpressionUUID->"039c55b1-9cea-df46-a2fa-\
d0d5293142fb"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

